      "description": "Weltevrede sits on the cooler eastern slopes of the Banhoek Valley, where late-ripening reds hold acid longer than they do on the valley floor. Forty-one of the sixty-eight hectares are under vine, planted in blocks between 2004 and 2018, with Cabernet Sauvignon and Shiraz on the upper decomposed granite and Chardonnay on the lower alluvial soils. The cellar handles 320 tonnes a season and carries its own crush, press and 18 stainless tanks. The homestead is a restored 1920s farmhouse, and two cottages currently run as guest accommodation with an existing tourism consent. Water comes from a registered Dwars River abstraction plus three boreholes, and the entire vineyard is under drip. Sold as a going concern with the standing crop, cellar plant and irrigation infrastructure included.",
