      "description": "Grootvlei is a working beef unit on the sweetveld belt outside Bergville, carrying a commercial Nguni and Bonsmara cross herd. The land is divided into fourteen camps with water to every camp from two equipped boreholes and a gravity fed reticulation line off the upper spring. Carrying capacity is measured at 1 large stock unit per 3.2 hectares in a normal season. Infrastructure includes a full handling facility with crush, scale and loading ramp, a 90 tonne feed store, and 46 hectares of planted pasture under dryland. The homestead is a four bedroom face brick house with a separate manager's cottage and four staff units. Rainfall averages 780 mm and the farm has never been destocked for drought in the current owner's fifteen years. Sold with the fixed improvements; livestock negotiable separately.",
