      "description": "Rietfontein lies in the Waterberg, an hour north of Vaalwater on gravel, and is fully enclosed by 2.4 metre certified game fence. The property runs a plains game population including kudu, impala, waterbuck, zebra, blue wildebeest and giraffe, with a counted estimate of roughly 640 animals at the last aerial census. Income currently comes from a six suite thatched lodge with its own boma, a separate four bed hunting camp and a walk in cold room with a carcass rail. Twelve boreholes feed a network of drinking troughs and three pans hold water through most of the dry season. The bush is mixed broadleaf and thorn on sandy soil, with a rocky ridge running the northern boundary that gives the lodge its view. Sold as a going concern with the game, lodge contents and vehicles included.",
